Z||000000||sparks||10-23-2000||09:49 AM||||How concerned should I be to find my transaxle had no fluid in it when I drained it yesterday?<P>I just bought the car a week ago.  It had a clutch put in ~200 miles ago.  I'm guessing the person that did that didn't refill the transaxle since there appear to be no major leaks.<P>Soo, how closely should I watch it?  Is it realatively a tough transmission or will it die on me in 100 miles from now?  :^)<P>Thanks again.<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||9
Z||000001||sparks||10-23-2000||09:51 AM||||I forgot, it's an 85 w/ a 2.5L<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||1
Z||000002||StuGood||10-23-2000||10:16 AM||||Well, it lasted 200 miles so far.  Good thing you caught it so soon.  At this point, I would fill it up and hope for the best.  If you are so inclined, tell the people who put your clutch in what you found. Hopefully, they'll learn something from you.  <P>I doubt it will die 100 miles from now, especially if it hasn't given you any trouble so far.  Check for leaks at the axle seals.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sparks||10-23-2000||11:06 AM||||I don't know who put the clutch in it since the previous owner did it.<P>I could contact them and find out.  Maybe I should do that.<P>I filled it up and I'm hoping for the best...<P>It's not acted up since I've driven it, I put about 100 miles on it after I bought it before I caught this.  I shoulda checked it right away.  I'll be sure next time to check right away and not delay...<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>sparks||||reg||9
Z||000004||rogergarrison||10-23-2000||05:39 PM||||when i got my original chassis, i never noticed any axle leaks, so never checked it for prob 5,000 miles. anyway i put in new clutch and figured while it was apart id put in new axle seals. well there was no oil in it at all (410/4 speed) and hadnt been any for long time. i just filled it up and its been fine, Ive put almost 40K on it since and still fine, no noise, works great. So i wouldnt worry too much.||||reg||1
